% Test cases for the oxygen policy (oxygen.le): synthetic claims, one or two
% per criterion of LCD L33797 and Policy Article A52514.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base oxygen cases includes these resources:
    oxygen.

the knowledge base oxygen cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete first-month concentrator claim: Group I at rest, the study by
% the treating practitioner, the order, the face-to-face (E1390 is on the
% required list since April 2026), delivery.
scenario group_1_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the concentrator.
    the HCPCS code of the concentrator is "E1390".
    the concentrator is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-05-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the arterial PO2 of Ann taken at rest is 54 mm Hg.
    the blood gas study of Ann was performed by treating practitioner.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of Ann.
    the blood gas study of Ann was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the treating practitioner examined Ann for the concentrator in a face-to-face encounter on 2026-04-20.
    the order for the concentrator is dated 2026-04-25.
    the order for the concentrator is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the concentrator includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the concentrator includes order date.
    the order for the concentrator includes description of the item.
    the order for the concentrator includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the concentrator includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the concentrator was communicated to the supplier on 2026-04-26.
    the concentrator was delivered on 2026-05-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the concentrator.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% A saturation of 90 at rest, nothing else: no group.
scenario not_hypoxemic is:
    claim 1 is for the concentrator.
    the HCPCS code of the concentrator is "E1390".
    the concentrator is furnished to Ben.
    the residence of Ben is private residence.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the oxygen saturation of Ben taken at rest is 90 percent.
    the blood gas study of Ben was performed by laboratory.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of Ben.
    the blood gas study of Ben was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% The study was performed by the DME supplier: not a qualifying study.
scenario supplier_study is:
    claim 1 is for the concentrator.
    the HCPCS code of the concentrator is "E1390".
    the concentrator is furnished to Cy.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the oxygen saturation of Cy taken at rest is 86 percent.
    the blood gas study of Cy was performed by DME supplier.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of Cy.
    the blood gas study of Cy was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].

% Group II: a saturation of 89 with cor pulmonale.
scenario group_2 is:
    claim 1 is for the concentrator.
    the HCPCS code of the concentrator is "E1390".
    the concentrator is furnished to Dee.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 2.
    the oxygen saturation of Dee taken at rest is 89 percent.
    the medical record of Dee documents cor pulmonale.
    the blood gas study of Dee was performed by hospital.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of Dee.
    the blood gas study of Dee was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

