    the blood gas study of Hal was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A Group IV condition: a terminal illness not affecting breathing is a
% denial whatever else the record says.
scenario group_4 is:
    claim 1 is for the concentrator.
    the HCPCS code of the concentrator is "E1390".
    the concentrator is furnished to Ida.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the oxygen saturation of Ida taken at rest is 86 percent.
    the medical record of Ida documents terminal illness not affecting breathing.
    the blood gas study of Ida was performed by hospital.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of Ida.
    the blood gas study of Ida was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Ida is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].

% Month 4 for a Group II beneficiary: the repeat study on day 75 and a new
% order; and the same claim without the repeat study.
scenario group_2_month_4 is:
    claim 1 is for the concentrator.
    the HCPCS code of the concentrator is "E1390".
    the concentrator is furnished to Dee.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-08-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 4.
    the concentrator was delivered on 2026-05-01.
    the oxygen saturation of Dee taken at rest is 89 percent.
    the medical record of Dee documents cor pulmonale.
    the blood gas study of Dee was performed by hospital.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of Dee.
    the blood gas study of Dee was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the repeat blood gas study of Dee was performed on 2026-07-15.
    the repeat oxygen saturation of Dee is 88 percent.
    a new order for the concentrator is dated 2026-07-20.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

scenario group_2_month_4_no_repeat is:
    claim 1 is for the concentrator.
    the HCPCS code of the concentrator is "E1390".
    the concentrator is furnished to Dee.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-08-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 4.
    the concentrator was delivered on 2026-05-01.
    the oxygen saturation of Dee taken at rest is 89 percent.
    the medical record of Dee documents cor pulmonale.
    the blood gas study of Dee was performed by hospital.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of Dee.
    the blood gas study of Dee was performed at the time of need.
    the finding oxygen will improve the condition about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers [].

